  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41123-PROJECT-220235</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41123" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Boosting institutional partnerships for youth engagement in sustainable innovation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project derives from the longstanding collaboration established between UNIDO ITPO Italy and the Italian Autonomous Region Friuli Venezia Giulia (FVG) since the joint declaration signed together on 8th May 2015 and as a follow-up to the project #Innovation Bridge Trieste-Dubai 2020#.  The goal of this new project will be to tangibly support potential entrepreneurs, innovators, SMEs, start-ups, organizations and further relevant stakeholders from Italy, the United Arab Emirates, and Bahrain # with a special focus on youth and women&apos;s engagement # to highlight their innovative sustainable solutions and develop game-changing profitable business models, in order to unleash the true potential of their green and digital transformation and access global markets.  In this framework, UNIDO through ITPO Italy, as a capacity-builder and knowledge and expertise broker, in synergy with the Division of ITPOs and Institutional Partnerships (GLO/ITP) will enhance and facilitate international partnerships to enable the exchange of know-how for green and digital entrepreneurship development among Italy, United Arab Emirates, and Bahrain in order to contribute to the Sustainable Development Goals through Progress by Innovation.</narrative>
  </description>
